{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YQBtyuEWjG1vaENs8zAUxx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"check-ceremony-script.py — lint de scripts de cerimônia (PLAN-174 W2).\n3\t\n4\tDescoberta por PROPRIEDADE DE CONTEÚDO, nunca por glob de nome (debate\n5\tr1 F4: a classe `grep|tail` tinha ZERO ocorrências dentro do glob\n6\t`OWNER-*.sh` e 4 fora dele). Um candidato é todo `*.sh` sob as raízes\n7\tcom shebang bash E pelo menos uma operação de cerimônia no corpo\n8\t(gpg / git tag / gh release / npm publish / sentinel / approved.md /\n9\tVERDICT).\n10\t\n11\tRegras (catálogo W1, seção A — `.claude/plans/PLAN-174/catalog.md`):\n12\t  R1  BLOCKING  proveniência: sem marca AUTO-GENERATED e sem exceção\n13\t                explícita (`CEREMONY-LINT: handwritten-exception:`)\n14\t  R2  BLOCKING  `|| true` na MESMA linha de operação remota\n15\t                irreversível (gpg/git tag/git push/gh release/npm\n16\t                publish) — a forma semântica do P1 OWNER-GA-CUT.sh:721\n17\t  R2a ADVISORY  `|| true` cru (taxa publicada, nunca bloqueia)\n18\t  R3  BLOCKING  `grep … | tail` em parsing de VERDICT\n19\t  R4  BLOCKING  `git add` de diretório (`-A`/`--all`/`.`/`dir/`)\n20\t  R5  ADVISORY  cp/mv para destino em variável sem teste `-L` nas 5\n21\t                linhas anteriores (escrita através de symlink no\n22\t                DESTINO — round 25)\n23\t  R6  ADVISORY  `shasum/sha256sum -c` sem asserção de conjunto próxima\n24\t                (set-equality — classe S272)\n25\t  R8  BLOCKING  exec-bit no índice git (modo 100755) — classe\n26\t                reincidente (rounds 8/9/12 + fix-forwards S314)\n27\t  R9  BLOCKING  crase ou `$(` dentro de heredoc SEM aspas: o shell executa, mesmo\n28\t                num comentário do corpo (S363: `git switch -c` rodou no cwd do\n29\t                chamador). Item 14 (a) do backlog da 1.4.4. Cura no script: aspas\n30\t                no delimitador, ou calcular a variável antes do heredoc\n31\t  R10 ADVISORY  harness de shell (`test-*`, `rehearse-*`, `ensaio-*`) sem a regressão\n32\t                do repositório chamador (`caller_repo_guard`, item 14 (b))\n33\t\n34\tFP (AC reescrito pelo debate): zero-FP exigido SÓ das BLOCKING; resíduo\n35\thistórico = waiver pinado por sha256 do CONTEÚDO em\n36\t`ceremony-lint-waivers.json` (re-arma quando o arquivo muda), datado,\n37\tcom motivo; waiver por caminho NÃO existe. Baseline só encolhe.\n38\t\n39\tEscape hatch (padrão ADR-186, forma fixada pelo consenso):\n40\t`CEO_CEREMONY_LINT_UNLOCK=<sha256 do arquivo>` +\n41\t`CEO_CEREMONY_LINT_UNLOCK_REASON` OBRIGATÓRIO — sem motivo, o bloqueio\n42\té MANTIDO. O unlock é gravado no audit trail (fail-open) e vale só para\n43\to run corrente.\n44\t\n45\tAUTOLIMITAÇÃO (obrigatória — debate r1 F6): a saída SEMPRE carrega a\n46\tlinha declarando o que este lint NÃO cobre. Verde aqui nunca encurta a\n47\tpauta do rail sobre a seção B do catálogo.\n48\t\n49\tExit: 0 = sem blocking não-waivado e piso de descoberta satisfeito;\n50\t1 = blocking OU piso violado (fail-closed em INPUT); 3 = erro de\n51\tinfraestrutura do próprio lint (CI trata como vermelho).\n52\t\n53\tStdlib-only, Python >= 3.9.\n54\t\"\"\"\n55\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n56\t\n57\timport argparse\n58\timport hashlib\n59\timport json\n60\timport os\n61\timport re\n62\timport subprocess\n63\timport sys\n64\tfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional\n65\t\n66\tREPO_ROOT = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"..\", \"..\"))\n67\t\n68\tDISCOVERY_ROOTS = [\n69\t    \".claude/plans\",\n70\t    \".claude/scripts/local/historical\",\n71\t]\n72\tEXPLICIT_FILES = [\n73\t    \".claude/scripts/local/generate-ceremony.sh\",\n74\t]\n75\t\n76\tSHEBANG_RE = re.compile(r\"\\A#!\\s*(?:/bin/|/usr/bin/env\\s+)(?:ba)?sh\")\n77\tCEREMONY_OPS_RE = re.compile(\n78\t    r\"\\bgpg\\b|git tag|gh release|npm publish|sentinel|approved\\.md|VERDICT\"\n79\t)\n80\tIRREVERSIBLE_RE = re.compile(\n81\t    r\"\\bgpg\\b|git tag|git push|gh release|npm publish|gh api\"\n82\t)\n83\tOR_TRUE_RE = re.compile(r\"\\|\\|\\s*true\\b\")\n84\tGREP_TAIL_RE = re.compile(r\"grep[^\\n|]*\\|\\s*tail\\b\")\n85\tGIT_ADD_DIR_RE = re.compile(r\"git add\\s+(?:-A\\b|--all\\b|\\.(?:\\s|$)|\\S+/\\s*$|\\S+/\\s)\")\n86\tCP_MV_VARDEST_RE = re.compile(r\"\\b(?:cp|mv)\\b[^\\n]*\\s\\\"?\\$\\{?[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z_0-9]*\\}?\\\"?\\s*$\")\n87\tSYMLINK_TEST_RE = re.compile(r\"\\[\\s+-L\\b|test\\s+-L\\b\")\n88\tSHASUM_C_RE = re.compile(r\"(?:shasum|sha256sum)\\b[^\\n]*\\s-c\\b\")\n89\tSET_EQ_NEAR_RE = re.compile(r\"wc -l|comm\\b|sort\\b.*diff|diff\\b.*sort\")\n90\tHEREDOC_OPEN_RE = re.compile(\n91\t    r\"\"\"<<(-?)[ \\t]*(?:'([^'\\n]+)'|\"([^\"\\n]+)\"|(\\\\?)([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z_0-9]*))\"\"\")\n92\tHARNESS_NAME_RE = re.compile(r\"(?:^|/)(?:test|rehearse|ensaio)[-_][^/]*\\.sh$\")\n93\tCALLER_GUARD_MARK = \"caller_repo_guard\"\n94\tPROVENANCE_MARK = \"AUTO-GENERATED\"\n95\tEXCEPTION_MARK = \"CEREMONY-LINT: handwritten-exception:\"\n96\t\n97\tSELF_LIMITATION = (\n98\t    \"ceremony-lint cobre as classes sintáticas da seção A do catálogo; \"\n99\t    \"NÃO cobre retomada, idempotência, fronteira irreversível remota nem \"\n100\t    \"binding de evidência por conteúdo (seção B) — pauta permanente do rail.\"\n101\t)\n102\t\n103\tDEFAULT_WAIVERS = os.path.join(\n104\t    REPO_ROOT, \".claude\", \"scripts\", \"ceremony-lint-waivers.json\"\n105\t)\n106\t# Piso de descoberta (arquivos RASTREADOS): pinado no primeiro censo\n107\t# S316 (41 rastreados de 54 descobertos) e RE-PINADO na rodada 6 do\n108\t# re-pass da v1.4.0-rc.1 (S349, 2026-09-08): o piso ficou em 41 enquanto\n109\t# a descoberta chegou a 124 rastreados, e apagar um script deixava o gate\n110\t# verde sem inspecioná-lo — o valor e o CENSO do candidato, e toda\n111\t# remoção exige re-pinar conscientemente. Falha quando o conjunto\n112\t# ENCOLHE — a pergunta \"o guard vê o meu alvo?\" respondida em toda\n113\t# execução. Residual declarado (rc.1 condição 52): um piso por CONTAGEM\n114\t# aceita «tira um, põe um»; a cura estrutural é pinar o CONJUNTO.\n115\t# RE-PINADO na rodada 13 (2026-09-10): 127 rastreados no candidato — tres\n116\t# scripts de cerimonia entraram depois da rodada 6 e 124 deixava passar tres\n117\t# remocoes sem inspecao. Cada script novo reabre a folga ate o re-pin seguinte.\n118\tDEFAULT_FLOOR = 127\n119\t\n120\t\n121\tdef _sha256(path: str) -> str:\n122\t    h = hashlib.sha256()\n123\t    with open(path, \"rb\") as fh:\n124\t        for chunk in iter(lambda: fh.read(65536), b\"\"):\n125\t            h.update(chunk)\n126\t    return h.hexdigest()\n127\t\n128\t\n129\tdef _git_tracked_modes(root: str) -> Dict[str, str]:\n130\t    try:\n131\t        out = subprocess.run(\n132\t            [\"git\", \"-C\", root, \"ls-files\", \"--stage\"],\n133\t            capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30, check=False,\n134\t        ).stdout\n135\t    except Exception:\n136\t        return {}\n137\t    modes: Dict[str, str] = {}\n138\t    for line in out.splitlines():\n139\t        parts = line.split(None, 3)\n140\t        if len(parts) == 4:\n141\t            modes[parts[3]] = parts[0]\n142\t    return modes\n143\t\n144\t\n145\tdef discover(root: str) -> List[str]:\n146\t    \"\"\"Candidatos por propriedade de conteúdo (os.walk — vê dirs ocultos,\n147\t    ao contrário de glob.glob; achado do debate r1).\"\"\"\n148\t    found: List[str] = []\n149\t    roots = [os.path.join(root, r) for r in DISCOVERY_ROOTS]\n150\t    for base in roots:\n151\t        if not os.path.isdir(base):\n152\t            continue\n153\t        for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(base):\n154\t            for fn in filenames:\n155\t                if not fn.endswith(\".sh\"):\n156\t                    continue\n157\t                p = os.path.join(dirpath, fn)\n158\t                try:\n159\t                    with open(p, errors=\"replace\") as fh:\n160\t                        body = fh.read()\n161\t                except OSError:\n162\t                    found.append(p)  # ilegível = candidato (fail-closed)\n163\t                    continue\n164\t                if SHEBANG_RE.match(body) and CEREMONY_OPS_RE.search(body):\n165\t                    found.append(p)\n166\t    for rel in EXPLICIT_FILES:\n167\t        p = os.path.join(root, rel)\n168\t        if os.path.isfile(p):\n169\t            found.append(p)\n170\t    return sorted(set(found))\n171\t\n172\t\n173\tdef _heredoc_openers(line: str) -> List[tuple]:\n174\t    \"\"\"``(delimitador, tira_tabs, expande)`` de cada heredoc aberto nesta linha de\n175\t    código. Anda a linha com o estado de aspas: `<<` numa string, num comentário, numa\n176\t    conta `$(( ))` ou num here-string `<<<` não abre heredoc.\"\"\"\n177\t    found: List[tuple] = []\n178\t    quote = \"\"\n179\t    i = 0\n180\t    while i < len(line):\n181\t        ch = line[i]\n182\t        if quote:\n183\t            if ch == \"\\\\\" and quote == '\"':\n184\t                i += 2\n185\t                continue\n186\t            if ch == quote:\n187\t                quote = \"\"\n188\t            i += 1\n189\t        elif ch in \"'\\\"\":\n190\t            quote = ch\n191\t            i += 1\n192\t        elif ch == \"\\\\\":\n193\t            i += 2\n194\t        elif ch == \"#\" and (i == 0 or line[i - 1] in \" \\t;|&(\"):\n195\t            break\n196\t        elif line.startswith(\"<<<\", i):\n197\t            i += 3\n198\t        elif line.startswith(\"<<\", i) and line.count(\"((\", 0, i) <= line.count(\"))\", 0, i):\n199\t            m = HEREDOC_OPEN_RE.match(line, i)\n200\t            if m is None:\n201\t                i += 2\n202\t                continue\n203\t            word = m.group(2) or m.group(3) or m.group(5)\n204\t            found.append((word, m.group(1) == \"-\", not (m.group(2) or m.group(3) or m.group(4))))\n205\t            i = m.end()\n206\t        else:\n207\t            i += 1\n208\t    return found\n209\t\n210\t\n211\tdef _expands_command(line: str) -> bool:\n212\t    \"\"\"Crase ou `$(` que o shell executaria (paridade de contrabarras respeitada).\"\"\"\n213\t    i = 0\n214\t    while i < len(line):\n215\t        if line[i] == \"\\\\\":\n216\t            i += 2\n217\t            continue\n218\t        if line[i] == \"`\" or line.startswith(\"$(\", i):\n219\t            return True\n220\t        i += 1\n221\t    return False\n222\t\n223\t\n224\tdef _heredoc_findings(lines: List[str]) -> List[dict]:\n225\t    \"\"\"R9, um achado por linha do corpo. Ponto cego declarado: string de várias linhas\n226\t    com `<<` dentro desalinha o estado de aspas (resíduo vira waiver, como os demais).\"\"\"\n227\t    findings: List[dict] = []\n228\t    pending: List[tuple] = []\n229\t    for i, ln in enumerate(lines, 1):\n230\t        if pending:\n231\t            word, strip_tabs, expands = pending[0]\n232\t            if (ln.lstrip(\"\\t\") if strip_tabs else ln) == word:\n233\t                pending.pop(0)\n234\t            elif expands and _expands_command(ln):\n235\t                findings.append({\"rule\": \"R9\", \"sev\": \"BLOCKING\", \"line\": i,\n236\t                                 \"msg\": \"crase ou $( executa dentro de heredoc sem aspas \"\n237\t                                        \"(delimitador %s)\" % word})\n238\t            continue\n239\t        pending.extend(_heredoc_openers(ln))\n240\t    return findings\n241\t\n242\t\n243\tdef lint_file(path: str, rel: str, git_mode: Optional[str]) -> List[dict]:\n244\t    findings: List[dict] = []\n245\t    try:\n246\t        with open(path, errors=\"replace\") as fh:\n247\t            body = fh.read()\n248\t    except OSError as exc:\n249\t        return [{\"rule\": \"R0\", \"sev\": \"BLOCKING\", \"line\": 0,\n250\t                 \"msg\": f\"ilegível ({exc}) — input fail-closed\"}]\n251\t    lines = body.splitlines()\n252\t\n253\t    if PROVENANCE_MARK not in body and EXCEPTION_MARK not in body:\n254\t        findings.append({\"rule\": \"R1\", \"sev\": \"BLOCKING\", \"line\": 1,\n255\t                         \"msg\": \"sem marca AUTO-GENERATED e sem exceção explícita\"})\n256\t    for i, ln in enumerate(lines, 1):\n257\t        if OR_TRUE_RE.search(ln):\n258\t            if IRREVERSIBLE_RE.search(ln):\n259\t                findings.append({\"rule\": \"R2\", \"sev\": \"BLOCKING\", \"line\": i,\n260\t                                 \"msg\": \"`|| true` sobre operação remota irreversível\"})\n261\t            else:\n262\t                findings.append({\"rule\": \"R2a\", \"sev\": \"ADVISORY\", \"line\": i,\n263\t                                 \"msg\": \"`|| true` cru\"})\n264\t        if GREP_TAIL_RE.search(ln):\n265\t            findings.append({\"rule\": \"R3\", \"sev\": \"BLOCKING\", \"line\": i,\n266\t                             \"msg\": \"grep|tail em parsing de VERDICT\"})\n267\t        if GIT_ADD_DIR_RE.search(ln):\n268\t            findings.append({\"rule\": \"R4\", \"sev\": \"BLOCKING\", \"line\": i,\n269\t                             \"msg\": \"git add de diretório\"})\n270\t        if CP_MV_VARDEST_RE.search(ln):\n271\t            ctx = \"\\n\".join(lines[max(0, i - 6):i - 1])\n272\t            if not SYMLINK_TEST_RE.search(ctx):\n273\t                findings.append({\"rule\": \"R5\", \"sev\": \"ADVISORY\", \"line\": i,\n274\t                                 \"msg\": \"cp/mv p/ destino em variável sem teste -L próximo\"})\n275\t        if SHASUM_C_RE.search(ln):\n276\t            ctx = \"\\n\".join(lines[max(0, i - 4):min(len(lines), i + 3)])\n277\t            if not SET_EQ_NEAR_RE.search(ctx):\n278\t                findings.append({\"rule\": \"R6\", \"sev\": \"ADVISORY\", \"line\": i,\n279\t                                 \"msg\": \"shasum -c sem asserção de conjunto (set-equality)\"})\n280\t    findings.extend(_heredoc_findings(lines))\n281\t    if HARNESS_NAME_RE.search(rel) and CALLER_GUARD_MARK not in body:\n282\t        findings.append({\"rule\": \"R10\", \"sev\": \"ADVISORY\", \"line\": 1,\n283\t                         \"msg\": \"harness sem a regressão do repositório chamador\"})\n284\t    # R8 só na superfície de binding assinado (.claude/plans/): exec-bit\n285\t    # em ferramenta de scripts/local/ é legítimo (invocada diretamente).\n286\t    if git_mode == \"100755\" and rel.startswith(\".claude/plans/\"):\n287\t        findings.append({\"rule\": \"R8\", \"sev\": \"BLOCKING\", \"line\": 0,\n288\t                         \"msg\": \"exec-bit no índice git (modo 100755)\"})\n289\t    return findings\n290\t\n291\t\n292\tdef _emit_unlock_audit(sha: str, reason: str) -> None:\n293\t    \"\"\"Advisory, fail-open: emissor canônico; senão, breadcrumb durável.\n294\t\n295\t    RESTAURADO (S318, pack SENT-S318 — o mesmo pack que registrou a ação\n296\t    ``ceremony_lint_unlock_used`` nas DUAS fontes canônicas que o gate\n297\t    ``check-audit-registry-coverage.py`` exige: ``_KNOWN_ACTIONS`` em\n298\t    ``.claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py`` e a tabela por-ação de\n299\t    ``SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md``). Histórico: o PLAN-174 W1 (7d467a8)\n300\t    embarcou este emissor SEM a metade canônica do registro, o gate pegou o\n301\t    órfão (6 jobs vermelhos), e a S317 (908707e) parcou o emit fixando a\n302\t    regra \"um emissor não embarca antes do registro dele\" — precedente\n303\t    v2.51 / SENT-GK-F.\n304\t\n305\t    Wire metadata-only (LLM06): ``file_sha256`` = prefixo 16-hex do sha256\n306\t    do script destravado; ``reason_len`` = comprimento do\n307\t    ``CEO_CEREMONY_LINT_UNLOCK_REASON``. O TEXTO do motivo nunca vai ao\n308\t    log — fica só no stderr do operador (abaixo).\n309\t\n310\t    Fail-open em TODA rota (um unlock advisory nunca pode quebrar o lint):\n311\t    emissor indisponível ⇒ breadcrumb durável em ``audit-log.errors`` — o\n312\t    mesmo destino que a versão parcada usava — e o stderr sempre imprime.\n313\t    \"\"\"\n314\t    line = (f\"ceremony-lint UNLOCK usado sha={sha[:16]} \"\n315\t            f\"reason_len={len(reason)}\")\n316\t    try:\n317\t        sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(REPO_ROOT, \".claude\", \"hooks\"))\n318\t        from _lib import audit_emit  # type: ignore\n319\t        fn = getattr(audit_emit, \"emit_generic\", None)\n320\t        if callable(fn):\n321\t            # emit_generic takes **kwargs as TOP-LEVEL event fields — the\n322\t            # 7d467a8 shape (`fields={...}`) nested the payload under a\n323\t            # single \"fields\" key the scrub correctly drops (caught by the\n324\t            # S318 clone-sim; the parked emitter had never run live).\n325\t            fn(action=\"ceremony_lint_unlock_used\",\n326\t               file_sha256=sha[:16], reason_len=len(reason))\n327\t        else:\n328\t            crumb = getattr(audit_emit, \"_breadcrumb\", None)\n329\t            if callable(crumb):\n330\t                crumb(line)\n331\t    except Exception:\n332\t        try:\n333\t            from _lib import audit_emit as _ae  # type: ignore\n334\t            crumb = getattr(_ae, \"_breadcrumb\", None)\n335\t            if callable(crumb):\n336\t                crumb(line)\n337\t        except Exception:\n338\t            pass\n339\t    try:\n340\t        # Rail S318 (P2): o stderr do operador também fica dentro da\n341\t        # fronteira fail-open — um BrokenPipeError/encoding error aqui não\n342\t        # pode abortar o lint depois de um unlock válido.\n343\t        print(f\"ceremony-lint: UNLOCK usado sha={sha[:16]} motivo={reason!r}\",\n344\t              file=sys.stderr)\n345\t    except Exception:\n346\t        pass\n347\t\n348\t\n349\tdef main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n350\t    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog=\"check-ceremony-script\")\n351\t    ap.add_argument(\"--root\", default=REPO_ROOT,\n352\t                    help=\"raiz do repo (testes usam tmp dir)\")\n353\t    ap.add_argument(\"--waivers\", default=None,\n354\t                    help=\"path do JSON de waivers (default: ao lado do lint)\")\n355\t    ap.add_argument(\"--floor\", type=int, default=None,\n356\t                    help=f\"piso do conjunto RASTREADO descoberto (default {DEFAULT_FLOOR})\")\n357\t    ap.add_argument(\"--json\", action=\"store_true\")\n358\t    ap.add_argument(\"--list\", action=\"store_true\",\n359\t                    help=\"só imprime os arquivos descobertos (um por linha)\")\n360\t    ap.add_argument(\"--print-waiver-template\", action=\"store_true\",\n361\t                    help=\"emite entradas de waiver p/ os arquivos hoje em BLOCKING\")\n362\t    args = ap.parse_args(argv)\n363\t\n364\t    root = os.path.abspath(args.root)\n365\t    try:\n366\t        files = discover(root)\n367\t    except Exception as exc:  # infra do próprio lint\n368\t        print(f\"ceremony-lint: INFRA error na descoberta: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n369\t        return 3\n370\t\n371\t    modes = _git_tracked_modes(root)\n372\t    rels = {f: os.path.relpath(f, root) for f in files}\n373\t    tracked = [f for f in files if rels[f] in modes]\n374\t\n375\t    if args.list:\n376\t        for f in files:\n377\t            print(rels[f])\n378\t        return 0\n379\t\n380\t    waivers_path = args.waivers or (\n381\t        DEFAULT_WAIVERS if root == REPO_ROOT\n382\t        else os.path.join(root, \".claude\", \"scripts\", \"ceremony-lint-waivers.json\")\n383\t    )\n384\t    waived_shas = set()\n385\t    waiver_entries: List[dict] = []\n386\t    if os.path.isfile(waivers_path):\n387\t        try:\n388\t            waiver_entries = json.load(open(waivers_path))\n389\t            waived_shas = {w[\"sha256\"] for w in waiver_entries\n390\t                           if w.get(\"sha256\") and w.get(\"reason\") and w.get(\"date\")}\n391\t        except Exception as exc:\n392\t            print(f\"ceremony-lint: waivers ilegíveis ({exc}) — input fail-closed, \"\n393\t                  \"nenhum waiver aplicado\", file=sys.stderr)\n394\t\n395\t    unlock_sha = (os.environ.get(\"CEO_CEREMONY_LINT_UNLOCK\") or \"\").strip().lower()\n396\t    unlock_reason = (os.environ.get(\"CEO_CEREMONY_LINT_UNLOCK_REASON\") or \"\").strip()\n397\t\n398\t    report: List[dict] = []\n399\t    blocking_live = 0\n400\t    advisory_counts: Dict[str, int] = {}\n401\t    for f in files:\n402\t        sha = _sha256(f)\n403\t        findings = lint_file(f, rels[f], modes.get(rels[f]))\n404\t        waived = sha in waived_shas\n405\t        if not waived and unlock_sha and sha == unlock_sha:\n406\t            if unlock_reason:\n407\t                waived = True\n408\t                _emit_unlock_audit(sha, unlock_reason)\n409\t            else:\n410\t                print(\"ceremony-lint: CEO_CEREMONY_LINT_UNLOCK sem \"\n411\t                      \"CEO_CEREMONY_LINT_UNLOCK_REASON — bloqueio MANTIDO\",\n412\t                      file=sys.stderr)\n413\t        is_tracked = rels[f] in modes\n414\t        n_block = sum(1 for x in findings if x[\"sev\"] == \"BLOCKING\")\n415\t        for x in findings:\n416\t            if x[\"sev\"] == \"ADVISORY\":\n417\t                advisory_counts[x[\"rule\"]] = advisory_counts.get(x[\"rule\"], 0) + 1\n418\t        # O gate conta SÓ arquivos rastreados: o CI clona o repo e nunca\n419\t        # vê untracked/gitignored (ponto cego DECLARADO no catálogo —\n420\t        # reportado no relatório, nunca fingido como coberto).\n421\t        if n_block and not waived and is_tracked:\n422\t            blocking_live += n_block\n423\t        report.append({\"file\": rels[f], \"sha256\": sha, \"tracked\": rels[f] in modes,\n424\t                       \"waived\": waived, \"findings\": findings})\n425\t\n426\t    floor = args.floor if args.floor is not None else DEFAULT_FLOOR\n427\t    floor_ok = len(tracked) >= floor\n428\t\n429\t    if args.print_waiver_template:\n430\t        tmpl = [{\"sha256\": r[\"sha256\"], \"path_hint\": r[\"file\"],\n431\t                 \"reason\": \"PREENCHER\", \"date\": \"PREENCHER\"}\n432\t                for r in report\n433\t                if any(x[\"sev\"] == \"BLOCKING\" for x in r[\"findings\"])\n434\t                and not r[\"waived\"]]\n435\t        print(json.dumps(tmpl, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n436\t        return 0\n437\t\n438\t    result = {\n439\t        \"discovered_total\": len(files),\n440\t        \"discovered_tracked\": len(tracked),\n441\t        \"floor\": floor,\n442\t        \"floor_ok\": floor_ok,\n443\t        \"blocking_unwaived\": blocking_live,\n444\t        \"advisory_rates\": advisory_counts,\n445\t        \"waivers_active\": len(waived_shas),\n446\t        \"self_limitation\": SELF_LIMITATION,\n447\t        \"files\": report,\n448\t    }\n449\t    if args.json:\n450\t        print(json.dumps(result, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n451\t    else:\n452\t        print(f\"ceremony-lint: {len(files)} descobertos \"\n453\t              f\"({len(tracked)} rastreados; piso {floor} \"\n454\t              f\"{'OK' if floor_ok else 'VIOLADO'})\")\n455\t        for r in report:\n456\t            for x in r[\"findings\"]:\n457\t                tag = \"waived\" if r[\"waived\"] and x[\"sev\"] == \"BLOCKING\" else x[\"sev\"]\n458\t                print(f\"  [{x['rule']}/{tag}] {r['file']}:{x['line']} — {x['msg']}\")\n459\t        print(f\"blocking não-waivado: {blocking_live} | advisory: {advisory_counts} \"\n460\t              f\"| waivers ativos: {len(waived_shas)}\")\n461\t        print(SELF_LIMITATION)\n462\t    return 0 if (blocking_live == 0 and floor_ok) else 1\n463\t\n464\t\n465\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n466\t    sys.exit(main())\n467\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"261e4768-bfba-44df-8655-b8fb9a3eb93f","uuid":"3c261030-f0e2-422a-9d18-98b4f165a9a3","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:51:22.816Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/scripts/check-ceremony-script.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"check-ceremony-script.py — lint de scripts de cerimônia (PLAN-174 W2).\n\nDescoberta por PROPRIEDADE DE CONTEÚDO, nunca por glob de nome (debate\nr1 F4: a classe `grep|tail` tinha ZERO ocorrências dentro do glob\n`OWNER-*.sh` e 4 fora dele). Um candidato é todo `*.sh` sob as raízes\ncom shebang bash E pelo menos uma operação de cerimônia no corpo\n(gpg / git tag / gh release / npm publish / sentinel / approved.md /\nVERDICT).\n\nRegras (catálogo W1, seção A — `.claude/plans/PLAN-174/catalog.md`):\n  R1  BLOCKING  proveniência: sem marca AUTO-GENERATED e sem exceção\n                explícita (`CEREMONY-LINT: handwritten-exception:`)\n  R2  BLOCKING  `|| true` na MESMA linha de operação remota\n                irreversível (gpg/git tag/git push/gh release/npm\n                publish) — a forma semântica do P1 OWNER-GA-CUT.sh:721\n  R2a ADVISORY  `|| true` cru (taxa publicada, nunca bloqueia)\n  R3  BLOCKING  `grep … | tail` em parsing de VERDICT\n  R4  BLOCKING  `git add` de diretório (`-A`/`--all`/`.`/`dir/`)\n  R5  ADVISORY  cp/mv para destino em variável sem teste `-L` nas 5\n                linhas anteriores (escrita através de symlink no\n                DESTINO — round 25)\n  R6  ADVISORY  `shasum/sha256sum -c` sem asserção de conjunto próxima\n                (set-equality — classe S272)\n  R8  BLOCKING  exec-bit no índice git (modo 100755) — classe\n                reincidente (rounds 8/9/12 + fix-forwards S314)\n  R9  BLOCKING  crase ou `$(` dentro de heredoc SEM aspas: o shell executa, mesmo\n                num comentário do corpo (S363: `git switch -c` rodou no cwd do\n                chamador). Item 14 (a) do backlog da 1.4.4. Cura no script: aspas\n                no delimitador, ou calcular a variável antes do heredoc\n  R10 ADVISORY  harness de shell (`test-*`, `rehearse-*`, `ensaio-*`) sem a regressão\n                do repositório chamador (`caller_repo_guard`, item 14 (b))\n\nFP (AC reescrito pelo debate): zero-FP exigido SÓ das BLOCKING; resíduo\nhistórico = waiver pinado por sha256 do CONTEÚDO em\n`ceremony-lint-waivers.json` (re-arma quando o arquivo muda), datado,\ncom motivo; waiver por caminho NÃO existe. Baseline só encolhe.\n\nEscape hatch (padrão ADR-186, forma fixada pelo consenso):\n`CEO_CEREMONY_LINT_UNLOCK=<sha256 do arquivo>` +\n`CEO_CEREMONY_LINT_UNLOCK_REASON` OBRIGATÓRIO — sem motivo, o bloqueio\né MANTIDO. O unlock é gravado no audit trail (fail-open) e vale só para\no run corrente.\n\nAUTOLIMITAÇÃO (obrigatória — debate r1 F6): a saída SEMPRE carrega a\nlinha declarando o que este lint NÃO cobre. Verde aqui nunca encurta a\npauta do rail sobre a seção B do catálogo.\n\nExit: 0 = sem blocking não-waivado e piso de descoberta satisfeito;\n1 = blocking OU piso violado (fail-closed em INPUT); 3 = erro de\ninfraestrutura do próprio lint (CI trata como vermelho).\n\nStdlib-only, Python >= 3.9.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional\n\nREPO_ROOT = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"..\", \"..\"))\n\nDISCOVERY_ROOTS = [\n    \".claude/plans\",\n    \".claude/scripts/local/historical\",\n]\nEXPLICIT_FILES = [\n    \".claude/scripts/local/generate-ceremony.sh\",\n]\n\nSHEBANG_RE = re.compile(r\"\\A#!\\s*(?:/bin/|/usr/bin/env\\s+)(?:ba)?sh\")\nCEREMONY_OPS_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\bgpg\\b|git tag|gh release|npm publish|sentinel|approved\\.md|VERDICT\"\n)\nIRREVERSIBLE_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\bgpg\\b|git tag|git push|gh release|npm publish|gh api\"\n)\nOR_TRUE_RE = re.compile(r\"\\|\\|\\s*true\\b\")\nGREP_TAIL_RE = re.compile(r\"grep[^\\n|]*\\|\\s*tail\\b\")\nGIT_ADD_DIR_RE = re.compile(r\"git add\\s+(?:-A\\b|--all\\b|\\.(?:\\s|$)|\\S+/\\s*$|\\S+/\\s)\")\nCP_MV_VARDEST_RE = re.compile(r\"\\b(?:cp|mv)\\b[^\\n]*\\s\\\"?\\$\\{?[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z_0-9]*\\}?\\\"?\\s*$\")\nSYMLINK_TEST_RE = re.compile(r\"\\[\\s+-L\\b|test\\s+-L\\b\")\nSHASUM_C_RE = re.compile(r\"(?:shasum|sha256sum)\\b[^\\n]*\\s-c\\b\")\nSET_EQ_NEAR_RE = re.compile(r\"wc -l|comm\\b|sort\\b.*diff|diff\\b.*sort\")\nHEREDOC_OPEN_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\"\"<<(-?)[ \\t]*(?:'([^'\\n]+)'|\"([^\"\\n]+)\"|(\\\\?)([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z_0-9]*))\"\"\")\nHARNESS_NAME_RE = re.compile(r\"(?:^|/)(?:test|rehearse|ensaio)[-_][^/]*\\.sh$\")\nCALLER_GUARD_MARK = \"caller_repo_guard\"\nPROVENANCE_MARK = \"AUTO-GENERATED\"\nEXCEPTION_MARK = \"CEREMONY-LINT: handwritten-exception:\"\n\nSELF_LIMITATION = (\n    \"ceremony-lint cobre as classes sintáticas da seção A do catálogo; \"\n    \"NÃO cobre retomada, idempotência, fronteira irreversível remota nem \"\n    \"binding de evidência por conteúdo (seção B) — pauta permanente do rail.\"\n)\n\nDEFAULT_WAIVERS = os.path.join(\n    REPO_ROOT, \".claude\", \"scripts\", \"ceremony-lint-waivers.json\"\n)\n# Piso de descoberta (arquivos RASTREADOS): pinado no primeiro censo\n# S316 (41 rastreados de 54 descobertos) e RE-PINADO na rodada 6 do\n# re-pass da v1.4.0-rc.1 (S349, 2026-09-08): o piso ficou em 41 enquanto\n# a descoberta chegou a 124 rastreados, e apagar um script deixava o gate\n# verde sem inspecioná-lo — o valor e o CENSO do candidato, e toda\n# remoção exige re-pinar conscientemente. Falha quando o conjunto\n# ENCOLHE — a pergunta \"o guard vê o meu alvo?\" respondida em toda\n# execução. Residual declarado (rc.1 condição 52): um piso por CONTAGEM\n# aceita «tira um, põe um»; a cura estrutural é pinar o CONJUNTO.\n# RE-PINADO na rodada 13 (2026-09-10): 127 rastreados no candidato — tres\n# scripts de cerimonia entraram depois da rodada 6 e 124 deixava passar tres\n# remocoes sem inspecao. Cada script novo reabre a folga ate o re-pin seguinte.\nDEFAULT_FLOOR = 127\n\n\ndef _sha256(path: str) -> str:\n    h = hashlib.sha256()\n    with open(path, \"rb\") as fh:\n        for chunk in iter(lambda: fh.read(65536), b\"\"):\n            h.update(chunk)\n    return h.hexdigest()\n\n\ndef _git_tracked_modes(root: str) -> Dict[str, str]:\n    try:\n        out = subprocess.run(\n            [\"git\", \"-C\", root, \"ls-files\", \"--stage\"],\n            capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30, check=False,\n        ).stdout\n    except Exception:\n        return {}\n    modes: Dict[str, str] = {}\n    for line in out.splitlines():\n        parts = line.split(None, 3)\n        if len(parts) == 4:\n            modes[parts[3]] = parts[0]\n    return modes\n\n\ndef discover(root: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Candidatos por propriedade de conteúdo (os.walk — vê dirs ocultos,\n    ao contrário de glob.glob; achado do debate r1).\"\"\"\n    found: List[str] = []\n    roots = [os.path.join(root, r) for r in DISCOVERY_ROOTS]\n    for base in roots:\n        if not os.path.isdir(base):\n            continue\n        for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(base):\n            for fn in filenames:\n                if not fn.endswith(\".sh\"):\n                    continue\n                p = os.path.join(dirpath, fn)\n                try:\n                    with open(p, errors=\"replace\") as fh:\n                        body = fh.read()\n                except OSError:\n                    found.append(p)  # ilegível = candidato (fail-closed)\n                    continue\n                if SHEBANG_RE.match(body) and CEREMONY_OPS_RE.search(body):\n                    found.append(p)\n    for rel in EXPLICIT_FILES:\n        p = os.path.join(root, rel)\n        if os.path.isfile(p):\n            found.append(p)\n    return sorted(set(found))\n\n\ndef _heredoc_openers(line: str) -> List[tuple]:\n    \"\"\"``(delimitador, tira_tabs, expande)`` de cada heredoc aberto nesta linha de\n    código. Anda a linha com o estado de aspas: `<<` numa string, num comentário, numa\n    conta `$(( ))` ou num here-string `<<<` não abre heredoc.\"\"\"\n    found: List[tuple] = []\n    quote = \"\"\n    i = 0\n    while i < len(line):\n        ch = line[i]\n        if quote:\n            if ch == \"\\\\\" and quote == '\"':\n                i += 2\n                continue\n            if ch == quote:\n                quote = \"\"\n            i += 1\n        elif ch in \"'\\\"\":\n            quote = ch\n            i += 1\n        elif ch == \"\\\\\":\n            i += 2\n        elif ch == \"#\" and (i == 0 or line[i - 1] in \" \\t;|&(\"):\n            break\n        elif line.startswith(\"<<<\", i):\n            i += 3\n        elif line.startswith(\"<<\", i) and line.count(\"((\", 0, i) <= line.count(\"))\", 0, i):\n            m = HEREDOC_OPEN_RE.match(line, i)\n            if m is None:\n                i += 2\n                continue\n            word = m.group(2) or m.group(3) or m.group(5)\n            found.append((word, m.group(1) == \"-\", not (m.group(2) or m.group(3) or m.group(4))))\n            i = m.end()\n        else:\n            i += 1\n    return found\n\n\ndef _expands_command(line: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Crase ou `$(` que o shell executaria (paridade de contrabarras respeitada).\"\"\"\n    i = 0\n    while i < len(line):\n        if line[i] == \"\\\\\":\n            i += 2\n            continue\n        if line[i] == \"`\" or line.startswith(\"$(\", i):\n            return True\n        i += 1\n    return False\n\n\ndef _heredoc_findings(lines: List[str]) -> List[dict]:\n    \"\"\"R9, um achado por linha do corpo. Ponto cego declarado: string de várias linhas\n    com `<<` dentro desalinha o estado de aspas (resíduo vira waiver, como os demais).\"\"\"\n    findings: List[dict] = []\n    pending: List[tuple] = []\n    for i, ln in enumerate(lines, 1):\n        if pending:\n            word, strip_tabs, expands = pending[0]\n            if (ln.lstrip(\"\\t\") if strip_tabs else ln) == word:\n                pending.pop(0)\n            elif expands and _expands_command(ln):\n                findings.append({\"rule\": \"R9\", \"sev\": \"BLOCKING\", \"line\": i,\n                                 \"msg\": \"crase ou $( executa dentro de heredoc sem aspas \"\n                                        \"(delimitador %s)\" % word})\n            continue\n        pending.extend(_heredoc_openers(ln))\n    return findings\n\n\ndef lint_file(path: str, rel: str, git_mode: Optional[str]) -> List[dict]:\n    findings: List[dict] = []\n    try:\n        with open(path, errors=\"replace\") as fh:\n            body = fh.read()\n    except OSError as exc:\n        return [{\"rule\": \"R0\", \"sev\": \"BLOCKING\", \"line\": 0,\n                 \"msg\": f\"ilegível ({exc}) — input fail-closed\"}]\n    lines = body.splitlines()\n\n    if PROVENANCE_MARK not in body and EXCEPTION_MARK not in body:\n        findings.append({\"rule\": \"R1\", \"sev\": \"BLOCKING\", \"line\": 1,\n                         \"msg\": \"sem marca AUTO-GENERATED e sem exceção explícita\"})\n    for i, ln in enumerate(lines, 1):\n        if OR_TRUE_RE.search(ln):\n            if IRREVERSIBLE_RE.search(ln):\n                findings.append({\"rule\": \"R2\", \"sev\": \"BLOCKING\", \"line\": i,\n                                 \"msg\": \"`|| true` sobre operação remota irreversível\"})\n            else:\n                findings.append({\"rule\": \"R2a\", \"sev\": \"ADVISORY\", \"line\": i,\n                                 \"msg\": \"`|| true` cru\"})\n        if GREP_TAIL_RE.search(ln):\n            findings.append({\"rule\": \"R3\", \"sev\": \"BLOCKING\", \"line\": i,\n                             \"msg\": \"grep|tail em parsing de VERDICT\"})\n        if GIT_ADD_DIR_RE.search(ln):\n            findings.append({\"rule\": \"R4\", \"sev\": \"BLOCKING\", \"line\": i,\n                             \"msg\": \"git add de diretório\"})\n        if CP_MV_VARDEST_RE.search(ln):\n            ctx = \"\\n\".join(lines[max(0, i - 6):i - 1])\n            if not SYMLINK_TEST_RE.search(ctx):\n                findings.append({\"rule\": \"R5\", \"sev\": \"ADVISORY\", \"line\": i,\n                                 \"msg\": \"cp/mv p/ destino em variável sem teste -L próximo\"})\n        if SHASUM_C_RE.search(ln):\n            ctx = \"\\n\".join(lines[max(0, i - 4):min(len(lines), i + 3)])\n            if not SET_EQ_NEAR_RE.search(ctx):\n                findings.append({\"rule\": \"R6\", \"sev\": \"ADVISORY\", \"line\": i,\n                                 \"msg\": \"shasum -c sem asserção de conjunto (set-equality)\"})\n    findings.extend(_heredoc_findings(lines))\n    if HARNESS_NAME_RE.search(rel) and CALLER_GUARD_MARK not in body:\n        findings.append({\"rule\": \"R10\", \"sev\": \"ADVISORY\", \"line\": 1,\n                         \"msg\": \"harness sem a regressão do repositório chamador\"})\n    # R8 só na superfície de binding assinado (.claude/plans/): exec-bit\n    # em ferramenta de scripts/local/ é legítimo (invocada diretamente).\n    if git_mode == \"100755\" and rel.startswith(\".claude/plans/\"):\n        findings.append({\"rule\": \"R8\", \"sev\": \"BLOCKING\", \"line\": 0,\n                         \"msg\": \"exec-bit no índice git (modo 100755)\"})\n    return findings\n\n\ndef _emit_unlock_audit(sha: str, reason: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Advisory, fail-open: emissor canônico; senão, breadcrumb durável.\n\n    RESTAURADO (S318, pack SENT-S318 — o mesmo pack que registrou a ação\n    ``ceremony_lint_unlock_used`` nas DUAS fontes canônicas que o gate\n    ``check-audit-registry-coverage.py`` exige: ``_KNOWN_ACTIONS`` em\n    ``.claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py`` e a tabela por-ação de\n    ``SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md``). Histórico: o PLAN-174 W1 (7d467a8)\n    embarcou este emissor SEM a metade canônica do registro, o gate pegou o\n    órfão (6 jobs vermelhos), e a S317 (908707e) parcou o emit fixando a\n    regra \"um emissor não embarca antes do registro dele\" — precedente\n    v2.51 / SENT-GK-F.\n\n    Wire metadata-only (LLM06): ``file_sha256`` = prefixo 16-hex do sha256\n    do script destravado; ``reason_len`` = comprimento do\n    ``CEO_CEREMONY_LINT_UNLOCK_REASON``. O TEXTO do motivo nunca vai ao\n    log — fica só no stderr do operador (abaixo).\n\n    Fail-open em TODA rota (um unlock advisory nunca pode quebrar o lint):\n    emissor indisponível ⇒ breadcrumb durável em ``audit-log.errors`` — o\n    mesmo destino que a versão parcada usava — e o stderr sempre imprime.\n    \"\"\"\n    line = (f\"ceremony-lint UNLOCK usado sha={sha[:16]} \"\n            f\"reason_len={len(reason)}\")\n    try:\n        sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(REPO_ROOT, \".claude\", \"hooks\"))\n        from _lib import audit_emit  # type: ignore\n        fn = getattr(audit_emit, \"emit_generic\", None)\n        if callable(fn):\n            # emit_generic takes **kwargs as TOP-LEVEL event fields — the\n            # 7d467a8 shape (`fields={...}`) nested the payload under a\n            # single \"fields\" key the scrub correctly drops (caught by the\n            # S318 clone-sim; the parked emitter had never run live).\n            fn(action=\"ceremony_lint_unlock_used\",\n               file_sha256=sha[:16], reason_len=len(reason))\n        else:\n            crumb = getattr(audit_emit, \"_breadcrumb\", None)\n            if callable(crumb):\n                crumb(line)\n    except Exception:\n        try:\n            from _lib import audit_emit as _ae  # type: ignore\n            crumb = getattr(_ae, \"_breadcrumb\", None)\n            if callable(crumb):\n                crumb(line)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n    try:\n        # Rail S318 (P2): o stderr do operador também fica dentro da\n        # fronteira fail-open — um BrokenPipeError/encoding error aqui não\n        # pode abortar o lint depois de um unlock válido.\n        print(f\"ceremony-lint: UNLOCK usado sha={sha[:16]} motivo={reason!r}\",\n              file=sys.stderr)\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n\ndef main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog=\"check-ceremony-script\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--root\", default=REPO_ROOT,\n                    help=\"raiz do repo (testes usam tmp dir)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--waivers\", default=None,\n                    help=\"path do JSON de waivers (default: ao lado do lint)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--floor\", type=int, default=None,\n                    help=f\"piso do conjunto RASTREADO descoberto (default {DEFAULT_FLOOR})\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--json\", action=\"store_true\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--list\", action=\"store_true\",\n                    help=\"só imprime os arquivos descobertos (um por linha)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--print-waiver-template\", action=\"store_true\",\n                    help=\"emite entradas de waiver p/ os arquivos hoje em BLOCKING\")\n    args = ap.parse_args(argv)\n\n    root = os.path.abspath(args.root)\n    try:\n        files = discover(root)\n    except Exception as exc:  # infra do próprio lint\n        print(f\"ceremony-lint: INFRA error na descoberta: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 3\n\n    modes = _git_tracked_modes(root)\n    rels = {f: os.path.relpath(f, root) for f in files}\n    tracked = [f for f in files if rels[f] in modes]\n\n    if args.list:\n        for f in files:\n            print(rels[f])\n        return 0\n\n    waivers_path = args.waivers or (\n        DEFAULT_WAIVERS if root == REPO_ROOT\n        else os.path.join(root, \".claude\", \"scripts\", \"ceremony-lint-waivers.json\")\n    )\n    waived_shas = set()\n    waiver_entries: List[dict] = []\n    if os.path.isfile(waivers_path):\n        try:\n            waiver_entries = json.load(open(waivers_path))\n            waived_shas = {w[\"sha256\"] for w in waiver_entries\n                           if w.get(\"sha256\") and w.get(\"reason\") and w.get(\"date\")}\n        except Exception as exc:\n            print(f\"ceremony-lint: waivers ilegíveis ({exc}) — input fail-closed, \"\n                  \"nenhum waiver aplicado\", file=sys.stderr)\n\n    unlock_sha = (os.environ.get(\"CEO_CEREMONY_LINT_UNLOCK\") or \"\").strip().lower()\n    unlock_reason = (os.environ.get(\"CEO_CEREMONY_LINT_UNLOCK_REASON\") or \"\").strip()\n\n    report: List[dict] = []\n    blocking_live = 0\n    advisory_counts: Dict[str, int] = {}\n    for f in files:\n        sha = _sha256(f)\n        findings = lint_file(f, rels[f], modes.get(rels[f]))\n        waived = sha in waived_shas\n        if not waived and unlock_sha and sha == unlock_sha:\n            if unlock_reason:\n                waived = True\n                _emit_unlock_audit(sha, unlock_reason)\n            else:\n                print(\"ceremony-lint: CEO_CEREMONY_LINT_UNLOCK sem \"\n                      \"CEO_CEREMONY_LINT_UNLOCK_REASON — bloqueio MANTIDO\",\n                      file=sys.stderr)\n        is_tracked = rels[f] in modes\n        n_block = sum(1 for x in findings if x[\"sev\"] == \"BLOCKING\")\n        for x in findings:\n            if x[\"sev\"] == \"ADVISORY\":\n                advisory_counts[x[\"rule\"]] = advisory_counts.get(x[\"rule\"], 0) + 1\n        # O gate conta SÓ arquivos rastreados: o CI clona o repo e nunca\n        # vê untracked/gitignored (ponto cego DECLARADO no catálogo —\n        # reportado no relatório, nunca fingido como coberto).\n        if n_block and not waived and is_tracked:\n            blocking_live += n_block\n        report.append({\"file\": rels[f], \"sha256\": sha, \"tracked\": rels[f] in modes,\n                       \"waived\": waived, \"findings\": findings})\n\n    floor = args.floor if args.floor is not None else DEFAULT_FLOOR\n    floor_ok = len(tracked) >= floor\n\n    if args.print_waiver_template:\n        tmpl = [{\"sha256\": r[\"sha256\"], \"path_hint\": r[\"file\"],\n                 \"reason\": \"PREENCHER\", \"date\": \"PREENCHER\"}\n                for r in report\n                if any(x[\"sev\"] == \"BLOCKING\" for x in r[\"findings\"])\n                and not r[\"waived\"]]\n        print(json.dumps(tmpl, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n        return 0\n\n    result = {\n        \"discovered_total\": len(files),\n        \"discovered_tracked\": len(tracked),\n        \"floor\": floor,\n        \"floor_ok\": floor_ok,\n        \"blocking_unwaived\": blocking_live,\n        \"advisory_rates\": advisory_counts,\n        \"waivers_active\": len(waived_shas),\n        \"self_limitation\": SELF_LIMITATION,\n        \"files\": report,\n    }\n    if args.json:\n        print(json.dumps(result, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n    else:\n        print(f\"ceremony-lint: {len(files)} descobertos \"\n              f\"({len(tracked)} rastreados; piso {floor} \"\n              f\"{'OK' if floor_ok else 'VIOLADO'})\")\n        for r in report:\n            for x in r[\"findings\"]:\n                tag = \"waived\" if r[\"waived\"] and x[\"sev\"] == \"BLOCKING\" else x[\"sev\"]\n                print(f\"  [{x['rule']}/{tag}] {r['file']}:{x['line']} — {x['msg']}\")\n        print(f\"blocking não-waivado: {blocking_live} | advisory: {advisory_counts} \"\n              f\"| waivers ativos: {len(waived_shas)}\")\n        print(SELF_LIMITATION)\n    return 0 if (blocking_live == 0 and floor_ok) else 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n","numLines":467,"startLine":1,"totalLines":467}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01YQBtyuEWjG1vaENs8zAUxx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
