{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7CNCUWwBstakEMr3JSN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found no P0 and no new P1 in payload 28/34, and no declared condition is false against this code. There are seven P2 follow-ups. I had no way to run code here, so everything below comes from reading the source.\n\n**Scope:** the tail of the `ceo-boot.py` split, the `ceo-cost-transcripts.py` split, the `ceo-restore.sh` hardening, the ceremony-lint waivers and R9/R10 rules, and changes to `check-active-hooks-executable.py`, `check-audit-real-loss.py` and `check-audit-registry-coverage.py`.\n\n**Conditions checked against this payload**\n- **3(b) holds.** `check-audit-real-loss.py:113-119` no longer crashes on a non-text `record_id`. The file goes into `malformed_record_id_files` (`:160`, `:208`) and raises an `attention` flag (`:269-270`). The exit code is unchanged.\n- **3(c) holds.** `check-audit-real-loss.py:67` turns off bytecode writing before the helper import at `:71`. `audit_spool_state.py:62` does the same before its `_lib` import at `:69`.\n- **7 holds.** Both scripts keep their paths and are now thin entry points over modules in `.claude/hooks/_lib/`.\n  - **ceo-boot:** every removed function reappears unchanged in `_ceo_boot_parts/candidates_lessons.py` (`:197`, `:279-495`) and `lessons_cli.py` (`:6`, `:132`). The parts run inside the script's own namespace, so `Path(__file__)` still finds `morning_ledger.py` and `lessons.py` in `.claude/scripts/`.\n  - **ceo-cost-transcripts:** the script imports every library name the parts use, so the moved functions resolve them and test patches still apply. The pricing tables are deep-copied, so each load gets its own copy.\n  - The installer copies `_lib` recursively and every `.claude/scripts/*.py`, so the new packages and `_restore_archive.py` reach installs (CHANGELOG `:342-346`). `_lib/**/*.py` is canonical-guarded (`guards.py:34`).\n  - The parts are standard library only and Python 3.9 compatible.\n- **The CHANGELOG's backup/restore and harness-gate lines (`:274-298`, `:320-323`) match the code.**\n- **Two P1 notes already signed with the rc still apply here** (they are declared, not new):\n  - claude-p27: `ceo-backup.sh:264` still keeps links with `cp -pR`, and `_restore_archive.py:112-113` still refuses any link member. The same refusal also hits older archives whose `memory/` contained links.\n  - claude-p06 P1-b: the redefinition at `ceo-boot.py:120` is never dispatched, because `_ceo_boot_parts/scheduled_cache.py:376` captures the copy in `model_persona.py:6`. The two bodies are the same today.\n\n**P2 follow-ups**\n1. **`repr()` of the cost-report records raises `NameError`** (`_cost_transcripts_parts/__init__.py:48-58`). When the loader rebuilds the dataclasses, it also re-points the `__repr__` wrapper that `dataclasses` generates. That wrapper looks up `_thread` (Python 3.9–3.12) or `get_ident` (3.13+), and neither name exists in the script's namespace. So `repr()` or `str()` of `UsageRecord`, `ScanCounters`, `PricingResult` or `Priced` raises. No production path prints these objects (CLI, `--json` and `collect()` read attributes), so only debugging and test-failure messages are hit. Fix: only re-point methods whose `__code__.co_filename` is the part file.\n2. **`ceo-restore.sh` now refuses a destination whose parent folder doesn't exist** (`:182-184`). Before, `mkdir -p` created it. On a new machine without `~/.claude/projects` (Scenario D in `DISASTER-RECOVERY.md:201-215`), or with `--dest /new/a/b`, restore exits 2 with \"destination parent must be a real directory\". The CHANGELOG doesn't mention this. Fix: refuse only links among the existing parents, then create the missing ones.\n3. **The apply prompt no longer lists what gets overwritten** (`ceo-restore.sh:302-304`). It names only `$DEST`, while `--restore-plans` and `--restore-agent-metrics` also overwrite files under `$(pwd)/.claude/`. Fix: put the per-target list back.\n4. **Stale exit codes and dead branches in `ceo-restore.sh`.** The header (`:15`) says a refused destination or SHA mismatch exits 1, but both exit 2 (`:191`, `:210`). The \"no .claude/ in CWD\" warnings (`:333-335`, `:348-350`) can no longer run, because the check at `:219-228` exits first.\n5. **The preview now writes the whole archive to temp** (`ceo-restore.sh:229-234`). It used to only list. A large backup can fill `/tmp` and make the preview fail with \"no space left\". Fix: validate only during preview and work out the targets from member names.\n6. **A comment now satisfies a source-text test** (`ceo-boot.py:180-184`). `test_plan_091_expected_callsites.py:138-143` passes on this comment, not on the real call site (now `scheduled_cache.py:326`). The comment also calls the test-only source check \"the delivery guard\". Fix: aim the test at the part file or at the runtime registry.\n7. **Minor items:**\n   - **Unknown hook type exits 2.** In `check-active-hooks-executable.py:165-166`, any hook type outside the table exits 2, which shows as a red harness check in an adopter's `/ceo-boot` if Claude Code adds a type. It is advisory only.\n   - **R9 false positive on a partly quoted heredoc delimiter.** `check-ceremony-script.py:90-91, 203-204` reads `<<E\"OF\"` as an unquoted delimiter `E` that never closes. Every later `$(` is then flagged as blocking (a false positive that fails closed, maintainer-only).\n   - **Waivers cover whole files.** The new waivers (`ceremony-lint-waivers.json:264-540`) waive every blocking rule in each pinned file, not just R9.\n   - **Stale docstring.** `ceo-cost-transcripts.py:32` still says the pricing table is \"below\" the docstring. It is now at `_cost_transcripts_parts/pricing.py:21`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7401,"cache_read_input_tokens":271943,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens"