member validation before extraction, physical --dest resolution, refusal of link targets and link ancestors, and one staged extraction shared by preview and apply.\n- Two signed rc lane notes are confirmed still present (they are declared, not new):\n  - claude-p27: ceo-backup.sh:264 still uses cp -pR for plans, and _restore_archive.py:112-113 refuses any link member. Older archives whose memory/ held links are refused the same way.\n  - claude-p06 P1-b: the redefinition at ceo-boot.py:120 is dead for dispatch, because scheduled_cache.py:376 captures the copy in model_persona.py:6. The two bodies are identical today.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): no undeclared P1 in this payload.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n1. P2 .claude/hooks/_lib/_cost_transcripts_parts/__init__.py:48-58. Class rebinding rebinds every method whose __module__ equals the part module. That includes the dataclasses-generated __repr__ wrapper: functools.wraps or reprlib copies __module__ from the exec-generated function. The wrapper's global _thread (Python 3.9-3.12) or get_ident (3.13+) does not exist in the script's namespace. So repr() or str() of UsageRecord, ScanCounters, PricingResult or Priced obtained from ceo-cost-transcripts raises NameError. No production path renders these objects (the CLI, --json and collect() read attributes), so only debug output and test-failure messages are affected. Minimal fix: rebind only methods whose __code__.co_filename is the part file, or skip dataclass-generated methods.\n2. P2 .claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:182-184. _physical_dest refuses a destination whose parent does not exist. The base code ran mkdir -p \"$DEST\". Scenario D of docs/DISASTER-RECOVERY.md:201-215 (new machine, no out-of-repo state, ~/.claude/projects not yet created), or any --dest or CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR under a missing folder, exits 2 with \"destination parent must be a real directory\". The CHANGELOG does not state this. Fix: walk to the nearest existing ancestor, refuse any link among the existing components, then mkdir -p (or document the requirement and say \"missing\" in the message).\n3. P2 ceo-restore.sh:302-304. The apply prompt now names only $DEST. With --restore-plans or --restore-agent-metrics it no longer says that files under $(pwd)/.claude/plans/ and $(pwd)/.claude/agent-metrics.md will be overwritten (the base listed them). Fix: put the per-target list back in the prompt.\n4. P2 ceo-restore.sh:13-16 against :191 and :210. The header maps \"SHA mismatch / refused destination\" to exit 1, but both exit 2. The \"no .claude/ in CWD\" branches at :330-335 and :340-350 can no longer run, because the preflight at :219-228 exits 2 first. Fix: align the header and remove or annotate the dead branches.\n5. P2 ceo-restore.sh:229-234. The preview, which only listed in the base, now extracts every accepted member into $TMPDIR. A large audit/ or plans/ backup can fill /tmp and fail the preview with ENOSPC. Fix: validate only in preview and derive the targets from member names, or document the disk use.\n6. P2 ceo-boot.py:180-184. The marker comment exists to satisfy source-text tests (tests/test_ceo_boot_audit_emit.py:95; hooks/tests/test_plan_091_expected_callsites.py:57,138-143). The EXPECTED_CALLSITES assertion \"ceo-boot.py must reference check_tier_policy_misrouting_24h\" is now met by a comment, not by the real call site at _ceo_boot_parts/scheduled_cache.py:326. The comment also calls a test \"the delivery guard\". Fix: point the check at the part file or at the runtime registry.\n7. P2 minor items:\n   (a) check-active-hooks-executable.py:165-166: a hook type outside _REQUIRED_FIELDS exits 2. Through check_harness_config.py:607-611 this shows as a RED harness_config_gate in an adopter's /ceo-boot if a later Claude Code adds a hook type (advisory, never session-blocking).\n   (b) check-ceremony-script.py:90-91,203-204: a partly quoted delimiter such as <<E\"OF\" is parsed as the unquoted delimiter E, which never closes, so every later \"$(\" is flagged R9 BL